# Catalan Accent Oracle

Research prototype: read-aloud Catalan → five macro-dialect similarity scores → comarca heatmap. **Not** geographic origin detection.

## Layout

- `web/` — React UI (Catalan copy)
- `backend/app.py` — FastAPI inference
- `scripts/` — ML pipeline
- `models/`, `data/`, `embeddings/` — gitignored local artifacts; classifier: `hf download miquelt-9/cv26-hubert-svm-calibrated --local-dir models/cv26-hubert-svm-calibrated`

## Dialect labels (fixed order)

`balearic`, `central`, `northern`, `northwestern`, `valencian`

## Conventions

- Minimal, focused diffs; match existing style
- Never commit secrets or large binaries
- Speaker-grouped train/eval splits
- Map: `web/public/map-oracle-linework.svg` + `DialectMap` / `ResultsMapStage` (linework stage; source geometry is `web/public/mapa-comarcal-accents.svg`)
- `comarcaMapMeta.ts` and `backend/comarques.py` are generated — rebuild both with `scripts/build_comarca_map.py`
- No IP or User-Agent is persisted; the self-declared comarca is the only geographic signal
- Observability: Sentry + Grafana OTLP via `backend/observability.py` / `web/src/lib/sentry.ts`; never send audio, bodies, comarca, or session/recording IDs (see README Observability)
- Inference: `backend/inference_pool.py` owns a fixed CPU-aware FIFO worker pool and bounded queue; configure with `ORACLE_WORKERS` and `ORACLE_MAX_QUEUE_SIZE`.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/ML_PIPELINE.md` for details.
